String Method / function in js

-> These are built - in function to manipulate a strings
-> this method are not change the oraginl string,  
but taking that and making a new string by using the method 

Types:-
. str.length                 // Returns the length of the string
. str.toUpperCase()          // Converts to uppercase
. str.toLowerCase()          // Converts to lowercase
. str.trim()                 // Removes whitespace from both ends
. str.trimStart()            // Removes whitespace from the beginning
. str.trimEnd()              // Removes whitespace from the end
. str.charAt(index)          // Returns the character at the given index
. str.at(index)              // Returns the character at the given index (supports negative index)
. str.indexOf(value)         // Returns the first index of the value
. str.lastIndexOf(value)     // Returns the last index of the value
. str.includes(value)        // Checks if the value exists
. str.startsWith(value)      // Checks if the string starts with the value
. str.endsWith(value)        // Checks if the string ends with the value
. str.slice(start, end)      // Extracts part of the string
. str.substring(start, end)  // Returns part of the string
. str.replace(old, new)      // Replaces the first matching value
. str.replaceAll(old, new)   // Replaces all matching values
. str.concat(str2)           // Joins two or more strings
. str.split(separator)       // Splits the string into an array
. str.repeat(count)          // Repeats the string
. str.padStart(length, char) // Pads the beginning of the string
. str.padEnd(length, char)   // Pads the end of the string
. str.search(value)          // Searches for a value and returns its index
. str.match(pattern)         // Returns matching values
. str.localeCompare(str2)    // Compares two strings
. str.valueOf()              // Returns the primitive string value
. str.toString()             // Converts to a string
